{"slug": "running-jasper-report-in-an-html-portlet-with-dynamic-filter-values", "title": "Jasper Report in an HTML Portlet with Dynamic Filters", "category": "Reporting", "categorySlug": "reporting", "date": "Oct 03, 2019", "author": "admin", "image": "https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262884/albatroz/blog/uploads/2023/06/reports.webp", "excerpt": "This blog post explains how a jasper report can be run from a PPM dashboard/page/tab like a portlet.", "readTime": 3, "content": "<ul class=\"post-info\">\n                                            <li style=\"list-style:none;padding-bottom:0\"></li>\n                                            <li style=\"list-style:none;padding-bottom:0\"></li>\n                                        </ul>\n                                    </div> -->\n                                    <div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><div class=\"vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid\"><div class=\"wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12\"><div class=\"vc_column-inner\"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n\t<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element\" >\n\t\t<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\n<p>Jasper reports in PPM can be run only from the Advanced Reporting section or from the Report &amp; Jobs section with the help of out of the box PPM capabilities. This blog post explains how a jasper report can be run from a PPM dashboard/page/tab like a portlet. The blog post also explains how the filter parameters on the report can be set dynamically.</p>\n<p><strong>Run Project Storyboard report as portlet in the Overview page:</strong></p>\n<p>To run a jasper report from PPM screen as a portlet, the report must be invoked using jasper report service with help of URL. As an example, we will use the Project Storyboard report. The following steps help in running the project storyboard report from the overview page with the help of HTML portlet.</p>\n<p>1. Create a new HTML portlet with the following code:<br />\n<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1708 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262827/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet1-768x681-1.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"681\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262827/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet1-768x681-1.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262825/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet1-768x681-1-300x266.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262826/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet1-768x681-1-62x55.webp 62w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262824/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet1-768x681-1-200x177.webp 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></p>\n<p>reportUnit can be modified to the complete path of the desired report.</p>\n<p>ParentFolderUri can be modified to the path of the path folder where the desired report is defined.<br />\n2. Click on Save and Return.<br />\n3. Add the HTML portlet to any tab on the Overview page.<br />\n4. When navigated to the respective page, the jasper report will be available to run as follows:<br />\n<img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1709 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262835/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput1-768x448-1.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"448\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262835/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput1-768x448-1.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262833/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput1-768x448-1-300x175.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262834/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput1-768x448-1-94x55.webp 94w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262832/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput1-768x448-1-200x117.webp 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></p>\n<p><strong>Run Project Storyboard report as with dynamic filters:</strong></p>\n<p>The following steps help you run the Project Storyboard report from the project properties page for the project in context alone.</p>\n<p>1. Create a new HTML portlet with the following code:</p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1711 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262831/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet2-768x708-1.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"708\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262831/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet2-768x708-1.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262829/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet2-768x708-1-300x277.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262830/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet2-768x708-1-60x55.webp 60w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262828/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/HTMLPortlet2-768x708-1-200x184.webp 200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /><br />\nHere the project internal id is fetched from the URL, stored in the variable prjID and passed to the report input control projectkey_1.<br />\nMultiple filters can be passed by appending the filter name and the value to the URL. For example,<br />\n/CSK_PRJ_ProjectStoryboard &amp;populateProject=1&amp;projectKey_1=500001<br />\nTo pass multiple values to a multi select filter in the report, the input control can be repeated with the respected values –<br />\n/CSK_PRJ_ProjectStoryboard &amp;populateProject=1&amp;projectKey_1=500001&amp; projectKey_1=500002<br />\nProperty output determines the output type of the report when it run. Valid output types are pdf, html, xls, xlsx, rtf, csv, docx<br />\n2. Click on Save and Return.<br />\n3. Add the HTML portlet to any of the project layout tabs. Here the portlet is added to a custom tab created under project layout –</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-1712 size-full\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262839/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput2-768x417-1.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"768\" height=\"417\" srcset=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262839/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput2-768x417-1.webp 768w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262838/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput2-768x417-1-300x163.webp 300w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262836/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput2-768x417-1-101x55.webp 101w, https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262837/albatroz/blog/uploads/2019/10/ReportOutput2-768x417-1-200x109.webp 200w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></p>\n\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n</div></div></div></div>\n</div>                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                            \n                            <div class=\"col-md-12\">\n                                <a href=\"https://albatrozsolutions.com/contact-us/\" style=\"margin-top: 15px;text-align:center;width: auto;\" class=\"banner-btn request_service_button pt-3 cta_btn\">Contact Us</a>\n                            </div>\n                             <div class=\"col-md-12\">\n                                <div class=\"social-share-btn\">\n                                                                        <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"share-btn-new clr-1\" href=\"https://x.com/intent/post?url=https%3A%2F%2Falbatrozsolutions.com%2Fblog%2Frunning-jasper-report-in-an-html-portlet-with-dynamic-filter-values%2F\"><img class=\"ex-icon\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/ddcx08e0s/image/upload/v1788262975/albatroz/blog/uploads/2024/06/twitter-1.png\" alt=\"Twitter Logo\"/><span>Tweet</span></a>\n                                    <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"share-btn-ne